# pall8t builds .pall8t/Containerfile with the project root as the build
# context (ADR-0010) so the Containerfile can COPY the repo-top flake files.
# Keep the context down to roughly what that COPY needs — without this,
# target/ (gigabytes) would be shipped to the builder on every image build.
#
# apple/container reads the ignore file from `<containerfile>.dockerignore`,
# next to the Containerfile named after it (BuildCommand.swift) — NOT from a
# `.dockerignore` at the context root, where docker would also look.
# Patterns are still relative to the context root (the project dir).
*
!flake.nix
!flake.lock
